    "result_text": "That's just JaCoCo coverage exclusions for generated code. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field. The field flows through the same generated-DTO + MapStruct pipeline as the other derived owner fields (`locality`, `timezone`, etc.):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getOwnerSegment()` getter (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java:464`). It composes `<TIER>_<AREA>`:\n   - **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when `getMembershipLevel() >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA**: `METRO` when `getLocality()` is a known region, else `REGIONAL`. I reused the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (keys `NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`) as the single source of known regions.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n**Tests:** The full suite (both acceptance tests \u2014 `STANDARD_METRO` for a known region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one) passes: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
