    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `getOwnerSegment()` is well-placed and idiomatic for this class:\n\n- It sits naturally alongside the other derived, `@Transient` getters (`getLocality`, `getTimezone`, `getDerivedMembershipLevel`), following the exact same pattern \u2014 a documented, read-only computed accessor over the owner's own fields.\n- Reusing `REGION_TIMEZONE.containsKey(getLocality())` for the AREA check is the right call rather than introducing a second literal set of `{NSW, VIC, QLD}`. That map is already the single source of truth for the canonical regions in this class, so `containsKey` avoids duplicating the region list and keeps the two region-dependent getters consistent.\n- TIER/AREA are computed locally with no new state, no new dependencies, and the method stays small and single-purpose \u2014 no catch-all growth.\n- The Javadoc and the OpenAPI `ownerSegment` schema entry mirror the surrounding `readOnly` field conventions, so the API surface stays uniform.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
